---
// Privacy Policy (Phase 4). ATTORNEY REVIEW: draft dated 2026-09-26 -- have
// counsel review within 30 days of launch (compliance.md rule 5) and before
// Phase 9 A2P 10DLC registration.
//
// Full A2P 10DLC element set (compliance.md rule 9), because GoHighLevel's
// Trust Center crawls this live URL at registration: SMS opt-in data
// collection/use, the fulfillment-only "no sharing" carve-out (bolded),
// cookies/tracking, data security, user rights, 18+.
//
// Call recording (Scott's decision, 2026-09-26): cite Utah's one-party rule
// (fact UT-003, Utah Code 77-23a-4) but commit to announcing recording at
// the start of every recorded call -- the portfolio's all-party-safe posture.
// The referral disclosure SENTENCE is not repeated here (footer only); the
// referral model is described where data sharing needs it.
import PageLayout from '../components/layout/PageLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site-config';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How St. George Elite Fence collects, uses and shares request details, including SMS consent, cookies, call recording, data security and your rights."
  path="/privacy-policy/"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  h1="Privacy Policy"
  lede="What we collect when you ask about a fence or wall project, who sees it, and what happens to your phone number and text-message consent."
  reviewed="2026-09-26"
  reviewedLabel="September 26, 2026"
>
  <h2 id="who-we-are">Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    This website, {site.domain}, is {site.brandName}, operated by {site.legalEntity}. We publish guides about fence and
    block-wall projects in the St. George, Utah area and, when a homeowner asks, pass the request to an independent fence or
    wall company that covers it. We do not build or repair fences or walls ourselves. In this policy, "we," "us," and "our"
    mean {site.brandName} and {site.legalEntity}; "you" means a visitor to this site or a person who sends us a request.
  </p>

  <h2 id="information-we-collect">Information we collect</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>What you give us.</strong> When you ask to be matched, you may give us your name, phone number, email address,
    city or ZIP code, the kind of project (for example a new fence, a repair, a block or retaining wall, or a pool fence),
    and details such as slope, HOA, or timing. If you call a phone number published on this site, we receive your phone
    number and the call details described below.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What is collected automatically.</strong> Our site and analytics tools record standard technical information:
    your IP address, browser and device type, the pages you view, the page or search that sent you here, and the date and
    time of your visit.
  </p>

  <h2 id="sms">Text messages and SMS opt-in data</h2>
  <p>
    Our request form includes an optional box you can check to agree to receive calls and text messages about your request
    from {site.brandName} and the independent company you are matched with. If you check it, we collect and keep your mobile
    number, the fact that you agreed, the exact consent wording shown to you, the date and time, and the page you used. We
    also keep a record of the messages we send and your replies, including STOP and HELP replies. We use this information
    only to send the messages you asked for and to show that you agreed to receive them. You do not have to check the box to
    send a request.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>We do not share mobile opt-in data or SMS consent with any third party or affiliate for marketing or promotional
    purposes. Your phone number is shared only with the specific independent company needed to fulfill your request, and it
    is never sold, rented, or shared for marketing.</strong> SMS opt-in data and consent records are excluded from every other
    category of sharing described in this policy.
  </p>

  <h2 id="how-we-use">How we use information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To match your request with an independent fence or wall company that covers your area and project type.</li>
    <li>To contact you about your request by phone, text, or email, consistent with the consent you gave.</li>
    <li>To keep records of your consent and of our messages with you.</li>
    <li>To operate, secure, and improve this site, including learning which guides are useful.</li>
    <li>To comply with the law and enforce our <a href="/terms-of-service/">Terms of Service</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="how-we-share">How we share information: fulfillment only</h2>
  <p>
    A referral cannot happen without sharing your request, so we share your contact details and project description with the
    specific independent company we match you with (and, if that company cannot take the job, with the next company we match
    you with), only so that company can contact you about the request you made. Beyond that:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>We do not sell personal information.</li>
    <li>We do not share SMS opt-in data or consent records with anyone for marketing.</li>
    <li>Service providers that host this site, run our forms, phone numbers, and contact records, and send messages for us process information only to provide those services to us.</li>
    <li>We may disclose information when the law requires it, to prevent fraud or abuse, or as part of a merger, acquisition, or sale of business assets, in which case this policy continues to apply.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The company you are matched with is an independent business. After it receives your request, its own privacy practices
    apply to how it uses your information.
  </p>

  <h2 id="cookies">Cookies and tracking technologies</h2>
  <p>
    This site uses cookies and similar technologies to work properly and to measure how it is used. We use Google Analytics
    to see which pages are visited and whether a visit led to a call or a request; Google handles that data under its own
    privacy policy. You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings, and Google offers a browser add-on that opts you
    out of Google Analytics. We do not run third-party advertising on this site and do not sell data to advertisers.
  </p>
  <p>
    This site is hosted and delivered by Cloudflare, which processes standard technical information (such as IP address and browser type) to serve and protect the site. Cloudflare may also load its Web Analytics script, which measures page views and loading speed without using cookies. Cloudflare processes that data under its own privacy policy.
  </p>

  <h2 id="call-recording">Phone calls and call recording</h2>
  <p>
    A phone number shown on this site may be a tracked number that forwards to us or to a matched company. We log call details
    such as the calling number, date, time, and length of the call. Calls may be recorded to confirm what was requested and to
    check service quality. No recording takes place until a live phone number is published on this site.
  </p>
  <p>
    Utah allows a call to be recorded with the consent of one party to it (<a href="https://le.utah.gov/xcode/Title77/Chapter23A/77-23a-S4.html" rel="noopener">Utah Code § 77-23a-4</a>).
    We do not rely on that rule alone: if a call is recorded, you will hear a notice at the start of the call. If you do not want
    to be recorded, tell us, end the call, or use the request form instead.
  </p>

  <h2 id="security">Data security</h2>
  <p>
    We use reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards to protect the information you give us. This site is
    served only over encrypted (HTTPS) connections, and access to request information is limited to the people and services that
    need it to handle your request. No website or storage system is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.
  </p>

  <h2 id="retention">How long we keep information</h2>
  <p>
    We keep request details and consent records as long as we need them to handle your request, to show that you consented, and
    to meet legal, tax, and dispute-resolution obligations. After that we delete them or remove the details that identify you.
  </p>

  <h2 id="your-rights">Your rights and choices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Stop texts:</strong> reply STOP to any text from us to stop receiving them. Reply HELP for help.</li>
    <li><strong>Access, correction, and deletion:</strong> ask what personal information we hold about you, and ask us to correct or delete it. We will do so unless the law requires us to keep it.</li>
    <li><strong>Stop other contact:</strong> ask us at any time to stop contacting you about anything other than a request you have in progress.</li>
    <li><strong>No sale:</strong> we do not sell personal information, so there is nothing to opt out of.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Send any of these requests through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. We may need to confirm your identity before we act
    on a request about your information.
  </p>

  <h2 id="children">Children</h2>
  <p>
    This site and its referral service are intended for adults 18 and older. We do not knowingly collect personal information from
    anyone under 18. If you believe a minor has sent us information, contact us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy from time to time. The "last reviewed" date above shows the latest version, and material changes will
    be posted on this page.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about this policy can be sent through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
</PageLayout>
